Emerald compiler 1.0.0

Usage:
  emeraldc [OPTIONS] file.rald
  emeraldc --repl [-I DIR]...

Compilation modes (choose at most one):
  --emit-tokens       print the lexer token stream
  --emit-ast          print the parser AST
  --emit-shapes       print tensor and dimension annotations
  --check             type-check without generating a binary
  --emit-c            print generated C instead of compiling it
  --repl              start the interactive compiler session

Diagnostics and checking:
  --json              emit diagnostics as JSON
  --proof             enable proof-mode checks
  --proof-report      print proof-mode measurements
  --shape-report      print shape solver measurements
  --werror            treat warnings as errors
  -Wno-CODE           suppress one warning code

Build options:
  -I DIR              add a module search directory
  -o OUT              choose the output binary path
  --keep-c            keep the generated .gen.c file
  -h, --help          show this help and exit
  -v, --version       print the compiler version and exit
